==Russian==
{{wp|ru:}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ru|pl|szabas}} from {{der|ru|yi|שבת||tr=shabes|Sabbath}}, from {{der|ru|he|שַׁבָּת|tr=shabát}}. {{doublet|ru|суббо́та}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|ша́баш}}
* {{ru-IPA|шаба́ш}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|ша́баш|or|шаба́ш}}

# [[Saturday]], observed in Judaism as a day of rest, [[Sabbath]].
# A meeting of witches, presided over by the devil, [[Sabbath]].
# Any merry debauched festival.
# {{lb|ru|colloquial}} end of the working day, [[quitting time]] (also pronounced šabáš).
#: {{ux|ru|'''Шабаш''', [[охотник|охо́тники]]! Сла́вно [[поработать|порабо́тали]]! — ве́село [[крикнуть|кри́кнул]] [[де́душка]]. — [[сейчас|Сейча́с]], пожа́луй, [[и]] домо́й [[пора́]].|"That’s it, hunters! We did a great job!" the grandfather shouted merrily. "Now it’s about time we went home."}}

